Changelog: 13-11-2026 19:01:22

Breaking. The Windows Portable Suite left Nexus for a repository of its own, github.com/RobertoTorino/windows-portable
(owner, 13-11-2026: one repository per suite, the tooling kept in Nexus for every suite). Its folder
`windows-portable/` is no longer in git here (`.gitignore` lists it), and its workflows `ci-windows-portable.yml`,
`release-windows-portable.yml` and `upstream-windows-portable.yml` are removed: the suite has its own `ci.yml`,
`release.yml` and `upstream.yml`. The suite keeps no copy of the tools. It is cloned into the Nexus checkout as
`windows-portable/`, where every tool finds it as before, and its workflows start each job with the new action
`.github/actions/suite`, which checks out Nexus at the commit the suite's `NEXUS_REF` names and the suite inside it.
`tools/suites.py` names the suites in a repository of their own (`OWN_REPOSITORIES`, `own_repository()`,
`of_repository()`). `tools/tag-release.sh` tags such a suite in its own repository and waits for its own `ci.yml`,
and `tools/ci_state.py` takes `--repo DIR` for the checkout a commit is of. `tools/nexus_release.py` leaves such a
suite off the Nexus release, and `release-nexus.yml` has no job for it. `release.yml` no longer excludes `wp-` tags.
`docs.yml` and `nexus-index.yml` check the suite out as its folder, so its wiki keeps its address and the index its
section; `docs.yml` also runs every night, for what the suite changed in its wiki. `tools/make_icons.py` writes the
suite's icons to its own `windows-portable/ICONS.md` (ICONS.md here written again without them) and its icon copies
only while the suite is in the checkout; `tools/make_design.py` checks the suite's stylesheet only then, and
`tools/features.py --check` checks the Apps and features chapter only where every suite it lists is in the checkout,
and says so. `tools/new_app.py` gives a Windows app's README the suite's own CI badge. `tools/ci-local.sh` leaves the
suite's folder out of its copy of the checkout, as GitHub's checkout of Nexus has none. The root
`requirements-dev.txt` no longer names the suite's folders: the suite has its own `requirements-dev.txt`. The tests
of the tools, Nexus Dashboard, Nexus Installer Tests and the Nexus Release Tool that are about the suite skip in a
checkout without it and run in the suite's CI. The README, the instruction files, MIGRATION.md (the plan, and what
is left for the BC250 suite's step) and the Nexus page's Development, Releases and GitHub settings chapters follow.

