Changelog: 12-11-2026 15:16:06

Added. tools/check_prose.py scores how hard the repository's text is to read and lists the files that need work
most, worst first. It reads the wikis, the READMEs and the text in the apps' windows, and counts long sentences,
semicolons, colons that carry a sentence on, long parentheses and listed words (British spelling, "manual" for the
wiki) per 1000 words. --details shows every finding with its line, and --base fails when a file reads worse than at
a commit. No workflow runs it yet. The Nexus page's Development chapter describes it.

